  "evidence_notes": "Monica, 27, was diagnosed with Crohn's last year after three years of symptoms. She also has PCOS and depression. She tried mesalamine with minimal help and prednisone for a flare, which caused weight gain. Azathioprine led to pancreatitis, and methotrexate caused unbearable nausea. Her doctor recommended biologics, and after an insurance battle, she was approved for Humira. She has injection anxiety but Humira is helping some, about 40% better. Her doctor suggests being more aggressive, but she is scared to switch. She is considering increasing Humira frequency, adding another drug, or switching biologics."
